static const char USAGE[] =
    "ELF32 little-endian MIPS symbol / debug-info dumper (pure stdlib).\n"
    "\n"
    "Usage:\n"
    "  python -I elf_symbols.py ELF OUT_DIR\n"
    "\n"
    "Writes into OUT_DIR:\n"
    "  symbols.txt       one line per .symtab symbol:\n"
    "                    address size type bind section raw_name demangled_name\n"
    "                    (header comments describe what was found; zero data lines\n"
    "                    if the ELF is stripped)\n"
    "  source_files.txt  STT_FILE entries plus, when the ELF has no symbol table,\n"
    "                    source-path strings found in the image (heuristic)\n"
    "  classes.txt       unique class / namespace qualifiers with member counts.\n"
    "                    From demangled symbols when available, otherwise from\n"
    "                    \"A::B::member\" strings found in the image (heuristic)\n"
    "  sections.txt      section table and debug-info presence report\n"
    "\n"
    "Demangling: auto-detects GNU v2 (GCC 2.x, \"Name__14CClassPC3Foo\") versus\n"
    "Itanium (\"_ZN...\") and implements a compact GNU v2 demangler (no templates\n"
    "beyond simple cases).  Itanium names are left as \"-\" (not implemented).\n"
    "\n";
